================================================================
Upstream sources and acknowledgements
================================================================

Most replayr readers were written from public format specifications,
primarily the TASVideos wiki's EmulatorResources pages and the
relevant emulators' own format-documentation pages. Out of an
abundance of caution -- because some readers cite the upstream
emulator source tree by name in their file headers, and the porting
process may have consulted that source -- replayr is licensed as
GPL-2+ to remain compatible with each upstream's terms.

The following five readers' file-header comments name the upstream
source code by file or tree name. We treat them as derivative work
of those upstream projects, all of which are GPL-2+:

----------------------------------------------------------------
1. Dolphin Emulator Project -- Dolphin (GameCube / Wii)
----------------------------------------------------------------

    Source:    https://github.com/dolphin-emu/dolphin
    License:   GNU General Public License v2 or later
    Citation:  R/read_dtm.R names "Dolphin source
               (Source/Core/Core/Movie.cpp)".

The .dtm GameCube movie format reader (R/read_dtm.R) was developed
with reference to Dolphin's `Source/Core/Core/Movie.cpp`. Wii .dtm
files are not supported.

----------------------------------------------------------------
2. PSXjin
----------------------------------------------------------------

    Source:    https://code.google.com/archive/p/psxjin/
               (and successor mirrors)
    License:   GNU General Public License v2 or later
    Citation:  R/read_pjm.R and R/read_pxm.R both name "the PSXjin
               source tree".

The .pjm (text body) and .pxm (binary body) movie format readers
were developed with reference to the PSXjin source tree.

----------------------------------------------------------------
3. lsnes
----------------------------------------------------------------

    Source:    https://github.com/Ilari-Pihlajisto/lsnes
               (and earlier mirrors)
    License:   GNU General Public License v2 or later
    Citation:  R/read_lsmv.R names "the lsnes source tree".

The .lsmv movie format reader (R/read_lsmv.R) was developed with
reference to the lsnes source tree alongside the TASVideos wiki at
/EmulatorResources/Lsnes/Movieformat.

----------------------------------------------------------------
4. VBA-rerecording
----------------------------------------------------------------

    Source:    https://github.com/TASEmulators/vba-rerecording
    License:   GNU General Public License v2 or later
    Citation:  R/read_vbm.R names "VBA-rerecording source (movie.h)".

The .vbm movie format reader (R/read_vbm.R) was developed with
reference to VBA-rerecording's `movie.h`.

